      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T00:31:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC ICO \"frames\" are independent from each other (can you confirm please?).  If so, then it seems that `kRestoreBGColor` may be more correct and efficient (e.g. by letting the embedder / client code know that it can discard the previous frame).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 282,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 282,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "d4d0e17c808a976522af0eb1516bcaa3b682aaf8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34fd45c2_ca68b221",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 4569768
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-16T15:42:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, ICO \"frames\" are fully independent.\n\nI changed kKeep to kRestoreBGColor. Combined with fRequiredFrame \u003d kNoFrame and fBlend \u003d kSrc, this correctly communicates that each ICO entry is fully independent and prior frame buffers can be discarded.",
      "parentUuid": "9cc7ea5b_60f6cbae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 282,
        "startChar": 66,
        "endLine": 282,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "d4d0e17c808a976522af0eb1516bcaa3b682aaf8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80e01f77_08fbf2f6",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T00:31:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we should also consider setting `embeddedOpts.fPriorFrame \u003d kNoFrame`?  I am not sure if this is necessary, but it seems that a frame index that is valid in the \"outer\" codec may become invalid in the \"inner\" codec, so therefore maybe it is better to set `fPriorFrame` to a safe value?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "d4d0e17c808a976522af0eb1516bcaa3b682aaf8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72962e3b_645ffb74",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_ico/decoder/impl/SkIcoRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 324,
      "author": {
        "id": 4569768
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-16T15:42:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right, thanks!\nThe prior frame could be something else, like 3, which is meaningless. We should set prior frame to kNoFrame.",
      "parentUuid": "80e01f77_08fbf2f6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 324,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 324,
        "endChar": 41
      },
